  "answer": "Go to the ER now. Call 911 if your child seems unwell. Fever with purple spots that don't fade when pressed needs urgent checking, even if your child looks well, because it can be a sign of a serious infection.",
  "triage": "Don't wait to see if the spots spread, and don't call 811 first. Call 911 now if your child is drowsy, floppy, hard to wake, breathing fast, or has a stiff neck. Otherwise go to the ER now and tell staff about the rash. 811 is for other questions, not this.",
  "sources": ["Royal Children's Hospital Melbourne", "Children's Health Queensland", "Connecticut Children's"]
}
